WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.700
Opening walkcast.kunjshah.in.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:16.950
It opens with “Paste a link. Get a video tour of your site. Nothing to film”. A real browser opens your site, signs in and clicks through your pages. The main button says “Download for Windows”.

3
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.740
It has a form asking for What a team of 5 people pays in.

4
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:35.090
Further down: You paste a link and it does the walking, Fast enough to re-run on every release, Loom films you and Records the pages only users see. Prices on the page include $0, $18 and $29.

5
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.550
Opening the download page.

6
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:47.440
The headline here reads “Download Walkcast. Free, version 0.8.1”. The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows may show "Windows protected your PC".

7
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:53.360
Scroll further and you’ll find Requirements, Windows SmartScreen, Uninstall and Linux.

8
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.520
Opening the lab page.

9
00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:10.510
This page leads with “Walkcast Lab. Why the browser agent failed, and the test that proves it”. Short answer: Walkcast Lab is browser agent testing for teams that build AI agents which drive a web browser. The button here reads “Download for Windows”.

10
00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:20.010
Below that: The problem with testing a browser agent, The vocabulary, Browser agent evals, in one page and How a failure becomes a regression test.

11
00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:24.740
That's the tour: 3 pages, recorded exactly as a visitor sees them.
